# React & Inertia Frontend

## File size

- Components and hooks **under 150 lines**. Extract subcomponents, hooks, or helpers early.
- Pages (`Pages/**`) compose feature components; avoid large inline forms/tables.

## Types & interfaces — never in component files

- Put types in `resources/js/types/` (or `types/<module>.ts`), not in `.tsx` component/page files.
- Components import types: `import type { Asset } from '@/types/asset'`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — types declared in AssetTable.tsx
interface AssetRow { id: number; name: string }
export function AssetTable({ rows }: { rows: AssetRow[] }) {}

// ✅ GOOD — types in types/asset.ts
import type { Asset } from '@/types/asset';
export function AssetTable({ assets }: { assets: Asset[] }) {}
```

## Naming

- Components: `PascalCase` files matching export (`AssetTable.tsx`).
- Hooks: `useAssetSearch`, not `useData` / `useX`.
- Event handlers: `handleSubmit`, `handleFolderSelect` — not `onClick1` / `fn`.

## Inertia patterns

- Initial page data from controller props only — no `useEffect` fetch on mount for page load.
- Mutations: `useForm` / `<Form>` for `web.php`; Axios (+ TanStack Query) only for `api.php` interactive calls.
- After AI save / move, prefer `router.reload({ only: ['assets'] })` over full navigation.

## Structure

```
Pages/          # screens only
Components/ui/  # shadcn primitives (do not hand-edit casually)
Components/<module>/  # feature UI
hooks/          # api.php wrappers
types/          # shared TS types
```

Keep JSX free of business rules that belong on the server (depth limits, ownership).
